# 1230 — 2024-12-30, uclibc 9.1.0

The drop the port runs on, and the only one proven on hardware.

## Release

    build_time     20241230152522 .. 152540   (modules)
    project_commit 8e24a5b
    sdk_commit     9e4d64f
    mhal_commit    da23dd9
    vermagic       5.10.61 preempt mod_unload ARMv7 thumb2 p2v8

Same vermagic as 0907, so insmod accepts either against this kernel and nothing
at load time catches a mismatched pair. The flavour is spelled out in the
directory name for that reason.

## Origin

Harvested from the camera's own shipped firmware -- a no-name SSC377QE with an
imx335 -- from `/config/modules/5.10/` on its second rootfs. Weaker provenance
than 0907 beside it, which came from the vendor release tree.

The userspace half is the `/config/lib` set in the same image, carried in
sigmastar-lib as `1230`. Both carry the triple above. Do not pair by the
vendor's own `script/demo.sh`, which puts a *different*, 2024-06 set on
LD_LIBRARY_PATH; see sigmastar-lib's PROVENANCE.

## One module, not nineteen

This drop ships the whole MI stack as a single `mi.ko`. 0907 ships 19 separate
`mi_*.ko` with a load order that matters.

    0907   19 modules   3746420 bytes   832 exported symbols
    1230    1 module    2522576 bytes   566 exported symbols

The smaller export count is not lost API. 301 of 0907's exports are absent
because they were only ever cross-module plumbing -- `MI_COMMON_AddResource`,
`MI_DEVICE_GetClass` and so on -- which a single object has no reason to export;
35 are new. The MI API userspace calls lives in the `.so` files, not here.

`depends=` is empty and there is no `mhal.ko`: everything the stack needs from
the vendor BSP is either inside this object or already built into the kernel.

It carries no `.debug_*` at all -- stripped by the vendor's own image build,
not by this repository. That is why the newer drop is the smaller one.

## Loading it

    insmod mi.ko g_ModParamPath=<modparam.json> \
                 drv_codec40_common.fw_load_path=<chagall.bin>
    insmod sensor_<sensor>_mipi.ko chmap=1

`g_ModParamPath` is registered bare; the VENC firmware parameter carries the
vendor's per-object prefix, as it does in 0907's separate `mi_vcodec.ko`. Both
have compiled-in `/config/...` defaults that thingino does not populate.

## Its sensor drivers are prebuilt, and must be

**This is the one drop whose sensors are not built from `sensor-src/`.**

`ms_cus_sensor` gained fields between release_0907 and this drop. Measured by
comparing the store offsets in our release_0907-built `sensor_imx335_mipi.ko`
against this image's own `imx335_MIPI.ko` -- both have exactly 115 distinct
offsets, so it is the same driver with a shifted struct rather than different
code:

    ours 2384  ->  oem 2392    +8
    ours 2496  ->  oem 2504    +8
    ours 2512  ->  oem 2524   +12
    ours 2620  ->  oem 2624    +4     pCus_sensor_GetVideoResNum

That last one is the same trap fe5d953 documents for the previous header: nothing
fails at load time, `Connect ... to sensor pad 0` still prints, and `mi_sensor`
reads its resolution count from the neighbouring slot and gets a plausible zero.
rvd then reports "sensor reports no modes" and no error is logged anywhere.

So the two drivers from the image are carried beside `mi.ko`, renamed to the
names `load_sigmastar` and raptor resolve by:

    imx335_MIPI.ko  ->  sensor_imx335_mipi.ko
    imx307_MIPI.ko  ->  sensor_imx307_mipi.ko

`soc/sigmastar/infinity6c.mk` sets `SIGMASTAR_SENSOR := prebuilt` for this drop,
which is what stops `sigmastar-sdk.mk` building `sensor-src/` and overwriting
them.

**Only these two sensors work on this drop.** The vendor release tree that would
carry the rest is not available for it, and the headers to rebuild the others
are not either. A board with any other sensor must use 0907 until that changes.

## Hardware

Proven on the SSC377QE above: 1080p H.264 at 25fps, single stream, no shims.
VIF DropCnt 0, ISP 25.00fps, SCL port0 FailCnt 0, VENC chn0 Fps_1s 25.00.

A second encoder channel still fails to bind, `MI_SYS_BindChnPort2` returning
`0xA0092008` for SCL port 1 -> VENC chn 1. That happens identically on 0907, so
it is not a property of either drop.

