# The runtime blobs are keyed by drop

`venc_fw/`, `iqfile/` and `sensor-iq/` used to sit at family level. They cannot:
all three are validated against the drop that reads them, and two of the three
fail loudly.

## venc_fw/ — the encoder rejects a foreign firmware

    0907   chagall.bin   249024 bytes   dfa6a803efce1a92f0386672f2dacdc4
    1230   chagall.bin   259904 bytes   68bd2cafe89c641ad027ddbb1bbe48cc

`mi.ko` checks it and says so:

    [ven-e][%s] fw ver:%llx mismatch driver:%llx, pls check fwVPU_if.h and
    chagall.bin/chagall.h in folder mhal/chip_commom/vcodec/hal/xxx/

## sensor-iq/ — the ISP rejects a foreign tuning

Per-sensor ISP API bins, magic `27 03 65 6d`, with a major version at offset 4
that the SDK checks:

    [MAJOR]: ispversion(%d) in sdk, ispversion(%d) in binfile.
    ooooops,SDK & iqbinfile major version is not match.

    0907   imx307 / imx335 / sc430ai    major 2
    1230   imx335                       major 5

A major-2 bin handed to the 2024-12 stack is rejected, and the ISP falls back to
generic tuning with visibly wrong colour rather than failing outright -- the
quiet failure of the three, which is why the version is recorded here.

1230's imx335 bin is this camera's own, from `/config/iqfile/imx335_iqfile.bin`
in the same image as the modules, so tuning and stack are matched for the first
time on this family. Contrast 0907's imx335 bin, which is OpenIPC's and matched
to nothing in particular (see below).

infinity6e's bins are magic `21 03 65 6d`, major 8 -- a different chip and a
different generation, which is why this key is per family as well as per drop.

## iqfile/ — CUS3A's default, paired with its own libcus3a

`iqfile0.bin` is a different format from the sensor-iq bins (no `27 03 65 6d`
magic) and carries no version field to check. It is keyed by drop on the same
grounds as the other two rather than on measured evidence: it is read at runtime
by that drop's own `libcus3a.so`.

    0907   iqfile0.bin   54175 bytes   the vendor's default
    1230   iqfile0.bin   54175 bytes   this camera's imx307 default

`isp_api.xml` sits beside it and differs between drops (194077 vs 209514 bytes).
Nothing reads it at runtime; it describes the ISP API to the vendor's tuning
tools.

