# sensor-src/

8 drivers and `include/`, all from release_0907, the same drop as that set of MI
modules. Source, compiled at build time. **Used by drop 0907 only** -- 1230
ships its own prebuilt drivers and says why above. Taken verbatim from

    ssc377/release_0907/sourcecode/sdk/driver/SensorDriver/
      drv/src/drv_ms_cus_<sensor>_MIPI.c   -> sensor_<sensor>_mipi.c
      drv/pub/{drv_ms_cus_sensor.h,sensor_i2c_api.h}
      drv/inc/{drv_sensor.h,drv_sensor_common.h,drv_sensor_init_table.h}

renamed to the module names load_sigmastar and raptor resolve by.

**These must come from the same drop as the MI modules, and the reason is not
obvious.** `ms_cus_sensor` is the handle the sensor driver fills and mi_sensor
reads, and its layout is not stable across releases: the header this tree
carried before had `app_spi_cfg spi_cfg` and `spi_handle_t *spi_bus` between
`i2c_bus` and `sensor_if_api`, which release_0907 does not. Two fields is enough
to move every callback after them. Built against the wrong header a driver still
compiles, still insmods -- vermagic only names the kernel -- and still prints
`Connect ... to sensor pad 0`, while mi_sensor reads its resolution count from
the neighbouring slot and gets a plausible zero. Verified by comparing all 42
`ms_cus_sensor` field offsets in the built module against the vendor's own
`imx335_MIPI.ko` from `project/release/chip/i6c/.../modules/5.10/`; they are
identical.

The same measurement against 1230's driver is what showed that drop needs its
own, so the rule has now caught two releases rather than one.

imx335 and imx415 were previously symlinks to infinity6e's copies, which is how
upstream ships them. They are real files here now because infinity6e is a
different drop for a different kernel, and sharing the source across the two
families is exactly what put the wrong struct in front of the 0907 modules.

sc4336p and sc501ai are dropped: release_0907 has no driver for either, and the
copies carried here came from a release whose headers the rest of this tree can
no longer be built against. No SigmaStar target selects them -- every sc4336p
config in thingino is Ingenic -- and against these MI modules they could not
have worked regardless.

Restored from cca10f4 when the family gained payload, having been removed in
4b08ea4 as an unreachable family.

