# The kernel pairing, now settled on hardware

johnchia/linux `sigmastar-infinity6c` at d17f67f is what the port runs. Its BSP
import, b335d21 "0000-infinity6c-kernel-5.10.61.patch", is authored by OpenIPC's
Viktor in November 2023 and sits directly on vanilla Linux 5.10.61 (230ca533).
It is not built from either drop carried here.

That was previously recorded as unverified. It is no longer: **drop 1230 loads
and streams on this kernel**, 1080p H.264 at 25fps on an SSC377QE. The argument
that it should work, kept because it is what made the attempt worth making:

  - Every sstar symbol these modules import is exported by the BSP. mi_sys.ko
    has 235 undefined symbols, 81 of them sstar; b335d21's drivers/sstar exports
    727, and all 81 are among them.
  - The one ABI-relevant header difference is inert here. b335d21's
    cam_os_struct.h sizes CAM_OS_RWTSEM_SIZE with an added
    sizeof(struct lock_class_key), which 0907's does not -- but that struct is
    `{ }` when lockdep is off, and every i6c defconfig leaves CONFIG_LOCKDEP
    unset, so both compute the same size.
  - The CamOs* declarations the sensor drivers bind to -- CamOsMemAlloc,
    CamOsMemRelease, CamOsPrintf, CamOsUsSleep -- are byte-identical between the
    two headers; only their line numbers moved. `mi.ko` exports none of them, so
    they come from the kernel.

**vermagic will not catch a mismatch**, which is why the whole flavour is in the
directory name: b335d21's i6c defconfig sets !SMP, PREEMPT, MODULE_UNLOAD and
THUMB2_KERNEL, composing exactly the string both drops carry --
`5.10.61 preempt mod_unload ARMv7 thumb2 p2v8` -- and CONFIG_MODVERSIONS is off.

Of the three SSC377 drops, release_0907 is the closest to this BSP by file count
(1183 identical BSP files against 1157 for 0712 and 1091 for 0602). That
corroborated the choice of 0907 at the time; note that it did not predict which
drop would actually stream, which was the newer one.

